Changelog: 07-10-2026 07:30:00

Uneven CU unlocks are now impossible, and the README explains the whole process for first-timers.

bc250-cu-unlock.sh: added validate_even(), which runs before any register is touched by both a bare
apply and --install. Only the three configurations that actually do something are accepted - 3 WGPs
on every shader-array row (24 CUs, stock), 4 on every row (32 CUs) or 5 on every row (40 CUs, max).
Anything uneven (e.g. 0x1f,0x1f,0x07,0x07 = 5/5/3/3) or at an unsupported level is refused with an
error naming the per-row counts and showing valid examples, instead of being written and persisted.
The GPU feeds all 4 arrays in lockstep, so such a mask only ever ran as fast as its smallest row
while drawing the extra power. Header docs and all usage examples updated to even masks.

bc250-cu-bisect.sh: the end-of-run suggestion no longer proposes a lopsided mask. The combined mask
of all good WGPs is trimmed down to the largest even level the board supports (dropping surplus WGPs
on the fuller rows), and both the retest command and the --install command it prints now use that
even mask. When a trim happened it says so, with the CU count you actually get.

bc250_unlock_gui/gate.py: the evenness check now also enforces the 3/4/5-WGPs-per-row levels, and the
rejection message includes the ready-to-run retest command for the even mask. Added even_level().
bc250_unlock_gui/main_window.py: the mask preview field marks a syntactically valid but uneven or
unsupported mask in orange with "not installable (needs 3, 4 or 5 WGPs on every row = 24/32/40 CUs)".
Placeholder masks in both GUIs changed to 0x0f,0x0f,0x0f,0x0f.

README.md: new "Unlocking extra CUs, step by step" section near the top - a plain-language, 7-step
walkthrough (prerequisites, bisect, read the suggestion, retest the combination, --install, verify
with --status, --uninstall) including what to expect in time and reboots, and a table of the only
three possible outcomes. The CU-layout note now states the 24/32/40 rule up front with that table,
and the persistence section shows the actual refusal message for an uneven mask.

Changelog: 05-10-2026 20:50:00

bc250-cu-bisect.sh and bc250_bisect_gui: raised the enforced minimums for a run - load time (-t)
is now 60s or more (was 30s), and rounds (-r) must be 2 or more unless --control-only is set, in
which case a single confirmation round is still allowed. Both the script and the GUI reject lower
values outright (the script re-checks even values restored from a saved config), the GUI's spin
boxes now also stop below these floors, and Rounds' floor lifts to 1 as soon as Control-only is
ticked. Also added to bc250_bisect_gui: a "Help" button (shows bc250-cu-bisect.sh's own --help
text) and a red "Reset" button (--reset) that requires an explicit confirmation popup warning that
all saved results and logs will be permanently deleted before it hands off to the terminal. Hovering
over any button, checkbox, combo box, spin box or line edit now shows a rounded box with a thin
Bazzite-purple (#8b4fd8) border, matching the accent used elsewhere in the project's GUIs.

Changelog: 05-10-2026 20:00:00

Added bc250_bisect_gui: a new PyQt6 menu-driven launcher for bc250-cu-bisect.sh's initial setup.
Lets you pick load time, rounds, a baseline variant (auto-detect, stock 24 CUs, fully unlocked 40
CUs, or custom), --control-only, --same-boot, --auto (unattended, with an option to also install
the systemd --user auto-resume unit) and --no-watch, then click "Start CU Bisect": the window
closes and the real run continues in a detected terminal emulator, exactly as if typed by hand.
Also added a "Show status" button (--status). This is a separate GUI from bc250_unlock_gui, which
is unchanged. Added packaging/bazzite/install-bisect-gui.sh and uninstall-bisect-gui.sh (same
venv-under-~/.local pattern as the unlock GUI installer) and packaging/common/bc250-cu-bisect.desktop,
plus a new README section documenting it. The launcher's own UI strings aren't translated yet
(unlike bc250_unlock_gui); a future iteration can add translations, a log-tailing view and an
inline --status view instead of a separate terminal.

Changelog: 05-10-2026 19:05:09

packaging/bazzite: renamed the installed GUI launcher/app dir from bc250-unlock-gui to
bc250-unlock-cu-gui, to avoid confusion with the sibling bc250-cores-bisect project's GUI
(bc250-cores-unlock-gui) and to make clear which unlock (CU vs. cores) it manages. Updated
install-gui.sh, uninstall-gui.sh, the .desktop Exec= line and the README accordingly. Anyone
with the old name already installed should run uninstall-gui.sh once, then install-gui.sh again
to pick up the new launcher name.

Changelog: 05-10-2026 07:00:46

images/bc250-cu-bisect.png: replaced the JPEG app icon with a PNG version. The source
bc250-cu-bisect.jpeg had a solid white background filling the corners outside the icon's
rounded-square shape; those corners are now flood-filled transparent (RGBA) instead of opaque
white, so the icon no longer shows a white box behind it when placed on a desktop/dock
background. Also resized from 1024x1024 to the standard 512x512 icon size. The old .jpeg was
removed in favor of the new bc250-cu-bisect.png.

Changelog: 04-10-2026 21:06:17

bc250-cu-bisect.sh: fixed a real `--auto` bug found while porting further hardening from the sibling
bc250-cores-bisect project. `ask()` wrote its "prompt -> auto: X" info line to stdout via `say`, which
command substitution (`$(ask ...)`) captured together with the actual answer - so e.g. "Continue
anyway? [y/N]" with default "y" produced a captured string that could never match `^[Yy]$`. In practice
this meant `--auto` silently `exit 0`'d at the very first pre-flight warning (governor MHz too high,
a non-memtest_vulkan load tool, missing GPU sysfs node, baseline/live mask mismatch - any one of these
common conditions), stopping the whole unattended run without telling you why. The info line now goes
to stderr; only the answer reaches stdout. Also hardened the sudo preflight: `sudo -v` is replaced with
`sudo -n true 2>/dev/null || sudo -v`, since `-v` can still prompt under a mixed sudoers (e.g. wheel
with password + a NOPASSWD drop-in) even though every command the script runs is already passwordless;
the keepalive loop uses the same `sudo -n true` check. Added an autostart-unit re-arm: a new `--auto`
run now re-enables `bc250-cu-bisect-auto.service` by itself if a previous finished run left it disabled
(via `auto_cleanup`), and warns up front if the unit isn't installed at all, instead of only discovering
after a reboot that nothing continued the run. Bumped VERSION to 1.2.3.

Changelog: 04-10-2026 20:06:10

bc250-cu-bisect.sh: hardened `--auto` based on the autorun service used in the sibling
bc250-cores-bisect project. `systemctl reboot` is now tried with `--no-ask-password` first and falls
back to `sudo -n systemctl reboot`, so an unattended run can't hang behind a GUI polkit auth popup
nobody is there to answer; if both fail the script stops with a clear message instead of hanging. Added
`auto_cleanup()`: once every attempt is done, `--auto` mode now disables
`bc250-cu-bisect-auto.service` and removes the optional live-output autostart entry by itself, so
nothing restarts at the next login (previously this had to be done by hand). The example systemd unit
now targets `default.target` instead of `graphical-session.target`, which gamescope/Steam sessions
don't always activate, and documents the optional desktop autostart entry for on-screen live output.
README's `--auto` section documents the new self-cleanup, the reboot fallback, and an unattended-run
checklist (autologin, credential popups). Bumped VERSION to 1.2.2.

Changelog: 04-10-2026 15:41:00

bc250-cu-unlock.sh: fixed the root cause of the unlock not surviving reboots. `--install` wrote
`ExecStart=$SELF` straight into the systemd unit - the path the script happened to be run from (e.g. a
git checkout under /home or /var/home). A root service executing from there fails at boot with a bare
"Permission denied" (SELinux denies exec on user_home_t from a system service; confirmed via
`systemctl status` showing status=203/EXEC), silently resetting to the stock 24 CUs every boot while
`--status` kept showing the configured masks as if nothing was wrong. `--install` now copies the script
to `/usr/local/sbin/bc250-cu-unlock.sh` (root-owned, 0755) and points the unit at that instead;
`--uninstall` removes it too. `--status` also now warns if the unit references a missing/stale copy, so
this failure mode is visible without needing to reboot and lose CUs to find out. Bumped VERSION to
1.1.2.

Changelog: 04-10-2026 15:25:00

bc250-cu-unlock.sh: fixed the `--status` "Service:" line wrongly appending "inactive" after the real
state (e.g. "enabled, failed inactive"). `systemctl is-active`/`is-enabled` exit non-zero for every
non-active/non-enabled state (failed, inactive, activating...) while still printing the correct state
word to stdout; the old `|| echo inactive` / `|| echo 'not installed'` fallbacks ran anyway and
concatenated a bogus word onto the real one. Now the fallback only fires when the command produced no
output at all (unit truly not installed/systemctl missing). Bumped VERSION to 1.1.1.

bc250_unlock_gui: `__version__` was hardcoded at "0.1.0" and never bumped despite many feature rounds
(gate logic, 8-language translations, GPLv3 relicense, UX polish), so the window title and About dialog
never reflected real progress. Bumped to 1.0.0, marking the current feature set as the first stable
release.

Changelog: 04-10-2026 15:20:00

bc250-cu-unlock.sh: fixed `find_umr()` checking `/fakebin/umr` three times (a copy-paste bug) instead of
the real install paths (`/usr/bin/umr`, `/usr/sbin/umr`, `/usr/local/bin/umr`). This made `--apply` and
the systemd unit it installs report "umr not found" even when umr was correctly installed via
`rpm-ostree install umr` and reachable with `which umr`. `bc250-cu-bisect.sh` already used the correct
path list and was not affected.

Changelog: 04-10-2026 13:30:00

bc250-cu-unlock.sh: --install no longer silently succeeds when it isn't actually persistent:
- `systemctl daemon-reload`, `systemctl enable` and a final `systemctl is-enabled` check are now all
  verified; any failure aborts with a clear error (pointing at `systemctl status`/`journalctl`) instead
  of printing "Installed and enabled" regardless of what actually happened. Previously a failed
  `systemctl enable` (e.g. SELinux, read-only /etc/systemd/system on some images) left the unlock
  applied only for the current boot, with no indication it wouldn't survive a reboot.
- The generated unit now also orders `After=sys-kernel-debug.mount`, in case the unlock runs before
  debugfs is mounted and umr can't find the GPU instance yet.
- `--status`'s "Installed masks" line renamed to "Configured masks" and now says explicitly it's only
  what's saved on disk, not proof the unlock is actually live - the "Live masks now" line (read straight
  from the GPU registers) is the authoritative one.
- Bumped VERSION to 1.1.0.

README: added a block on how to be certain of the live CU count when different tools disagree (this
project's own live register read vs. the bc250-bazzite-test-releases test #21 vs. third-party GPU info
tools that can show a driver-cached, stale CU count instead of a live one), plus a troubleshooting note
for an unlock that doesn't survive a reboot.

