bc250_unlock_gui CU map and banner polish:
- The CU-map header row (WGP0..WGP4) is now properly centered above its column of boxes.
- The ACCEPTED/NOT ACCEPTED banner heading is now left-aligned like the reason text below it,
  instead of centered.
- The WGP boxes in the CU map are wider (52px -> 64px) and no longer have a large, unintentional
  gap between the SE.SH row labels and the boxes.

README: added a worked example (uneven vs. even combined mask) under the GUI's acceptance rules,
reusing a real uneven-mask rejection scenario to show why the gate requires equal WGP counts on
all 4 rows.

Changelog: 03-10-2026 23:45:00

bc250-cu-bisect.sh --control-only:
- New flag: only runs the control item, skipping per-WGP bisecting entirely. For re-validating a
  combined mask you already bisected (e.g. after a full run to confirm the good WGPs still hold
  together) in a single boot, instead of also re-testing WGPs already known to be bad.
- The setting is remembered in the state dir like --rounds/--time, so it also applies across
  reboots for a resumed run.
- The script's own suggested "test the combination" command now includes --control-only.

