  description, the repository link and the license.
- The window remembers its size and position across restarts (QSettings), instead of always
  reopening at a fixed 640x520.
- New strings translated into the same 8 languages as before.

Changelog: 03-10-2026 22:49:00

bc250_unlock_gui UX polish:
- Gate status is now a full banner (red/white "NOT ACCEPTED YET!", green/white "ACCEPTED" once the
  retest passes), instead of a small coloured label.
- A wrong sudo password no longer dead-ends with a generic failure dialog: the password prompt reopens
  immediately with "Incorrect password, try again." and retries the same action, no need to re-click
  Install/Uninstall.
- Busy cursor + a "Working — installing/uninstalling…" label while a privileged action runs, so it's
  clear the app hasn't frozen; buttons have tooltips explaining what each one does.
- SudoDialog disables OK while the password field is empty instead of sending a blank password.
- All of the above newly-added strings are translated into the same 8 languages as before.

Changelog: 03-10-2026 22:20:00

Release automation + clarified persistence docs:
- .github/workflows/release.yml: real workflow (replaces the commented-out Android placeholder),
  triggered on every push to main. Auto-bumps a repo-wide VERSION (patch only, skipping any tag that
  already exists), tags the commit, builds a bc250-cu-bisect-vX.Y.Z.tar.gz with `git archive` (the whole
  toolset: both scripts, bc250_unlock_gui/, packaging/, images, docs) plus a .sha256 checksum, and
  publishes both as a GitHub Release via softprops/action-gh-release. Add "[skip-version]" to a commit
  message to skip releasing it.
- New top-level VERSION file (repo-wide release version, independent of each script's own -V output);
  .gitattributes export-ignores .github/.gitattributes/.gitignore from the release tarball.
- README: new "Releases" section; made explicit that bc250-cu-unlock.sh --install (and the GUI's
  Install) is persistent — the systemd service reapplies the mask on every boot with no further action,
  surviving reboots/power-offs/OS updates until --uninstall.

Changelog: 03-10-2026 22:10:00

bc250_unlock_gui — translations and a Bazzite installer:
- Full UI translation support: window/dialog text wrapped in self.tr(), QTranslator loads the system
  locale at startup (override with --lang <code>), real translations for es, fr, de, zh, ja, it, pl, ru
  under bc250_unlock_gui/translations/ (.ts sources + compiled .qm). Qt's own bundled qtbase_*.qm gives
  translated standard dialog buttons (Yes/No/OK/Cancel) for free. Compiling .ts -> .qm needs
  pyside6-lrelease at build time only (pip install PySide6-Essentials); the compiled .qm files are
  committed, so installing/running the GUI never needs PySide6.
- packaging/bazzite/install-gui.sh + uninstall-gui.sh: self-installer for Bazzite. Copies the app into a
  private venv under ~/.local/share/bc250-unlock-gui, adds a ~/.local/bin/bc250-unlock-gui launcher, a
  .desktop entry and icon — no rpm-ostree layering, user-scoped, fully reversible. Packages for other
  distros (rpm/PKGBUILD/deb) are deferred; only Bazzite has actually been tested.
- README: GUI section documents the Bazzite installer and --lang.

Changelog: 03-10-2026 21:49:00

bc250_unlock_gui 0.1.0 — optional GUI for bc250-cu-unlock.sh:
- New PyQt6 (>=6.11,<7) app, bc250_unlock_gui/, run with `python3 -m bc250_unlock_gui` from a venv
  (requirements.txt at the repo root). Mirrors the bc250-bazzite-test GUI's venv/QProcess/sudo pattern.
- gate.py reads bc250-cu-bisect.sh's own state (umr-config, umr-runs.tsv, umr-pending) and only enables
  Install once it proves the combined mask was retested as its own baseline (no WGPs left under
  individual test), every retest round passed, no attempt is mid-run, and the 4 rows are even — the
  same conditions the README asks for by hand. Explains exactly what's missing otherwise, with a
  "Re-check bisect results" button.
- A 4x5 CU grid lights up the accepted mask; Install/Uninstall run bc250-cu-unlock.sh through sudo
  (masked password dialog, passed to sudo -S only, never stored); Refresh status shows --status output
  without needing root.
- README: new "GUI" subsection under "Keeping the unlock after a reboot".

Changelog: 03-10-2026 21:31:00

1.2.0 — a way to keep a validated CU unlock after a reboot:
- bc250-cu-unlock.sh: new, standalone script. Reapplies a mask you've already validated with
  bc250-cu-bisect.sh (same umr register writes: CC_GC_SHADER_ARRAY_CONFIG, SPI_PG_ENABLE_STATIC_WGP_MASK,
  RLC_PG_ALWAYS_ON_WGP_MASK), every boot, as a root systemd service ordered before the display manager.
  It does not retest anything. --install <masks> saves + applies now + enables the service; --uninstall
  disables it (stock 24 CUs from the next boot); --status shows the installed masks, service state and
  live masks; plain `sudo ./bc250-cu-unlock.sh <masks>` applies once without persisting.
- bc250-cu-bisect.sh summary: once the combined mask is GOOD, also warns when the unlocked WGPs are
  uneven across the 4 SE.SH rows (no performance gain from the surplus until the other rows catch up),
  and suggests the matching `bc250-cu-unlock.sh --install` command.
- README: new "Keeping the unlock after a reboot" section.

Changelog: 03-10-2026 20:51:00

1.1.0 — a CU map during the run, and a way to stop clicking through reboots by hand:
- CU map: an ASCII/color grid of the 4 SE.SH rows x 5 WGPs (2 CUs each), shown at startup, before every
  attempt (highlighting the WGP under test), and in the summary/report. Marks baseline-unlocked WGPs,
  GOOD/FAILS EVERY TIME/RANDOM verdicts, and what's still untested. Colors turn off automatically for
  non-terminal output (e.g. the saved report file).
- --auto: skips every prompt (an unfinished attempt is assumed to be a crash, warnings are passed
  through) and reboots on its own when attempts remain, instead of asking. Still one attempt per boot,
  so no loss of isolation between attempts.
- bc250-cu-bisect-auto.service.example: a systemd --user unit that relaunches the script after every
  login, so the whole bisect runs unattended; only a real freeze still needs a manual power cycle.
  README documents the unit and the one sudoers NOPASSWD rule --auto needs (umr, journalctl).
- README: added the CU layout as an ASCII diagram (the default 24-CU grid, and a live/in-progress
  example with the >>/ok/xx/?? markers), and a note that unlocked WGPs must be kept even across the 4
  SE.SH rows — the GPU front-end splits work across all 4 in lockstep, so an uneven combined mask still
  boots and runs, it just won't give any more performance than the stock 24 CUs.

Changelog: 03-10-2026 15:00:00

1.0.0 — moved to its own repository (from bc250-bazzite-test) and rewritten: tells bad WGPs apart from
an unstable unlock, with its own unlock. No dependency on an external CU manager.
- Writes the masks itself with umr (CC/SPI/RLC registers of a runtime unlock), only on an idle GPU, and
  reads them back; during the load it reads them again every 10 s to catch drift.
- A control item does the same writes with the baseline masks (no extra CUs): if it fails, the unlock
  method, power or heat is at fault, not the CUs. Every locked WGP is then tested on its own.
- Several rounds per item (--rounds, default 3), interleaved; one attempt per boot by default
  (--same-boot restores the baseline live instead). A crash is detected on the next run, with the phase
  (writing the masks or under load) and the kernel faults of the previous boot.
- memtest_vulkan error reports count as failures (wrong results, not only crashes); max temperature,
  clock and GPU busy are recorded. Refuses to start when an unlock is already active at boot; warns about
  a governor ceiling above 1500 MHz.
- Verdict per WGP: GOOD, FAILS EVERY TIME (likely bad) or RANDOM (likely the unlock, power or heat), plus
  a combined mask of the good WGPs. --status, --reset, --version; report on the Desktop.
- Fixed: the old summary used the row name as an array index, so its suggested combined mask was wrong.
- New results files (umr-*.tsv) in ~/.local/share/bc250-cu-bisect; the old results.tsv is not used.

Changelog: 28-09-2026 22:35:00

First version (part of bc250-bazzite-test):
- Per-Shader-Array CU bisect helper: tests one extra WGP (+2 CUs) per array while the other three stay at
  the known-good baseline.
- Per step: the user applied the printed masks with an external CU manager; the script ran a stress load
  (memtest_vulkan/vkpeak/vkmark/glmark2), scanned the kernel log for GPU faults and asked about artifacts.
- Verdicts in ~/.local/share/bc250-cu-bisect/results.tsv: crash-safe, resumes after a hard hang. The final
  summary suggested a combined mask; a readable report was copied to the Desktop.
